question-capture/13964292/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77164" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the points $A(3t,t,4),$ $B(3t,4t,3)$ and $C(5t,t+1,5).$ Find $∠BAC$ given that $\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}=2.$ Round your answer to the nearest degree." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c138e79e69852f73c5d8d62bcc01cfaeaeb160d75072882928b7f2f20f0df35" "basis" 650 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77164" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the position vectors of the points $A,$ $B$ and $C$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=⟨3t,\\,t,\\,4⟩,\\,b=⟨3t,\\,4t,\\,3⟩,\\,c=⟨5t,\\,t+1,\\,5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠BAC=\\theta .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/assets/285b8343208079181ac6036cf9ca16abc974d59b9262878ed40c0da9af5683d0.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =⟨3t,\\,4t,\\,3⟩-⟨3t,\\,t,\\,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,3t,\\,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =⟨5t,\\,t+1,\\,5⟩-⟨3t,\\,t,\\,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t,\\,1,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}=2$, we can solve for $t,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =2 \\\\ 0\\cdot 2t+3t\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot 1 & =2 \\\\ 3t-1 & =2 \\\\ 3t & =3 \\\\ t & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨0,3,-1⟩, \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =⟨2,\\,1,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}}{|\\overset{\\to }{AB}||\\overset{\\to }{AC}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{10}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{2\\sqrt{15}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{15}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{15}})≈{75}^{∘}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c138e79e69852f73c5d8d62bcc01cfaeaeb160d75072882928b7f2f20f0df35" "basis" 650 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77164" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3c4ae64d9a3b82d1d472628be6b7d38a56c75262d035fbf1513196b1932ceac9" "basis" 650 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77164" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c138e79e69852f73c5d8d62bcc01cfaeaeb160d75072882928b7f2f20f0df35" "basis" 650 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77164" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{58}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/state.json" "file_sha256