ion-capture/13964292/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77164" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{75}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c138e79e69852f73c5d8d62bcc01cfaeaeb160d75072882928b7f2f20f0df35" "basis" 650 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4327" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the angle between $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 2,-1,1 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 1,5,-2 \\rangle$. Round your answer to $1$ decimal place." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/example-4327.json" "file_sha256" "d54021ef644f7b5a247e30e2c3fc9eb3555b9bc1c406195f79d008067ba64e20" "basis" 650 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-5112" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $\\mathbf{a}\\cdot \\mathbf{b}=-4$, find the angle between $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle t, \\, -2 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 6, \\, t \\rangle$. Round your answer to $1$ decimal place." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/example-5112.json" "file_sha256" "356ecf4df1339dc2a4c44a754ee592b1e87a838e992cfecdca401222768cfd31" "basis" 650 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-69833" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $∠XZY$ given the points $X(-1,0,3)$, $Y(-2,2,3)$, and $Z(-2,-1,3).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038738/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a640d249d816721c007b22d83d6a4adf87213239913229a7030d51d082d2aea" "basis" 1318 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038738/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-69833" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the position vectors of the points $X$, $Y$, $Z$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=⟨-1,0,3⟩,\\,y=⟨-2,2,3⟩,\\,z=⟨-2,-1,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $△XYZ$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠XZY=\\theta .$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038738/assets/87453fecb9da6b9e673ab5a85a289a3fac73f4fb90fc8f1b33e7c0a80b1ea77f.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{ZX}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{ZY}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{ZX} & =x-z \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,3⟩-⟨-2,-1,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,1,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{ZY} & =y-z \\\\  & =⟨-2,2,3⟩-⟨-2,-1,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,3,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{ZX}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{ZY}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{ZX}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{ZY}}{|\\overset{\\to }{ZX}||\\overset{\\to }{ZY}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 3+0\\cdot 0}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}}\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{3}^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}})={45}^{∘}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038738/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a640d249d816721c007b22d83d6a4adf87213239913229a7030d51d082d2aea" "basis" 1318 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038738/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-69833" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.diffi