rt/verification.json"} {"question" "q-101511" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{86}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f5561ca8a59b2eaedeef88d63f3cd36dea9b3abbe7b944cd99b6db533f584f7" "basis" 1409 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-101511" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{91}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f5561ca8a59b2eaedeef88d63f3cd36dea9b3abbe7b944cd99b6db533f584f7" "basis" 1409 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-124826" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $∠XZY$ given the points $X(-2,1,0)$, $Y(-1,0,4)$, and $Z(-1,2,-2).$ Round your answer to the nearest degree." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f5561ca8a59b2eaedeef88d63f3cd36dea9b3abbe7b944cd99b6db533f584f7" "basis" 1409 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-124826" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the position vectors of the points $X$, $Y$, $Z$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=⟨-2,1,0⟩,\\,y=⟨-1,0,4⟩,\\,z=⟨-1,2,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $△XYZ$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠XZY=\\theta .$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/assets/87453fecb9da6b9e673ab5a85a289a3fac73f4fb90fc8f1b33e7c0a80b1ea77f.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{ZX}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{ZY}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{ZX} & =x-z \\\\  & =⟨-2,1,0⟩-⟨-1,2,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,-1,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{ZY} & =y-z \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,4⟩-⟨-1,2,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-2,6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{ZX}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{ZY}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{ZX}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{ZY}}{|\\overset{\\to }{ZX}||\\overset{\\to }{ZY}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1)\\cdot 0+(-1)\\cdot (-2)+2\\cdot 6}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}}\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{6}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{40}} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{\\sqrt{240}} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{4\\sqrt{15}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{15}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{15}})={25}^{∘}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f5561ca8a59b2eaedeef88d63f3cd36dea9b3abbe7b944cd99b6db533f584f7" "basis" 1409 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-124826" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6ec99b73bd0e45287c6205dca701f4d8435e073bd05cb9cfc6c557ae7078ee9b" "basis" 1409 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-124826" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f5561ca8a59b2eaedeef88d63f3cd36dea9b3abbe7b944cd99b6db533f584f7" "basis" 1409 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-124826" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{21}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f5561ca8a59b2eaedeef88d63f3cd36dea9b3abbe7b944cd99b6db533f584f7" "basis" 1409 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-124826" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{23}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f5561ca8a59b2eaedeef88d63f3cd36dea9b3abbe7b944cd99b6db533f584f7" "basis" 1409 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-124826" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{25}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f5561ca8a59b2eaedeef88d63f3cd36dea9b3abbe7b944cd99b6db533f584f7" "basis" 1409 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-124826" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{28}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f5561ca8a59b2eaedeef88d63f3cd36dea9b3abbe7b944cd99b6db533f584f7" "basis" 1409 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-124826" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{30}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f5561ca8a59b2eaedeef88d63f3cd36dea9b3abbe7b944cd99b6db533f584f7" "basis" 1409 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77164" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the points $A(3t,t,4),$ $B(3t,4t,3)$ and $C(5t,t+1,5).$ Find $∠BAC$ given that $\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}=2.$ Round your answer to the nearest degree." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f5561ca8a59b2eaedeef88d63f3cd36dea9b3abbe7b944cd99b6db533f584f7" "basis" 1409 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77164" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the position vectors of the points $A,$ $B$ and $C$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=⟨3t,\\,t,\\,4⟩,\\,b=⟨3t,\\,4t,\\,3⟩,\\,c=⟨5t,\\,t+1,\\,5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠BAC=\\theta .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/assets/285b8343208079181ac6036cf9ca16abc974d59b9262878ed40c0da9af5683d0.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =⟨3t,\\,4t,\\,3⟩-⟨3t,\\,t,\\,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,3t,\\,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =⟨5t,\\,t+1,\\,5⟩-⟨3t,\\,t,\\,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t,\\,1,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}=2$, we can solve for $t,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =2 \\\\ 0\\cdot 2t+3t\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot 1 & =2 \\\\ 3t-1 & =2 \\\\ 3t & =3 \\\\ t & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨0,3,-1⟩, \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =⟨2,\\,1,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}}{|\\overset{\\to }{AB}||\\overset{\\to }{AC}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{10}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{2\\sqrt{15}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{15}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{15}})≈{75}^{∘}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f5561ca8a59b2eaedeef88d63f3cd36dea9b3abbe7b944cd99b6db533f584f7" "basis" 1409 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77164" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6ec99b73bd0e45287c6205dca701f4d8435e073bd05cb9cfc6c557ae7078ee9b" "basis" 1409 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77164" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f5561ca8a59b2eaedeef88d63f3cd36dea9b3abbe7b944cd99b6db533f584f7" "basis" 1409 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77164" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{58}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f5561ca8a59b2eaedeef88d63f3cd36dea9b3abbe7b944cd99b6db533f584f7" "basis" 1409 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77164" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{65}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f5561ca8a59b2eaedeef88d63f3cd36dea9b3abbe7b944cd99b6db533f584f7" "basis" 1409 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77164" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{75}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f5561ca8a59b2eaedeef88d63f3cd36dea9b3abbe7b944cd99b6db533f584f7" "basis" 1409 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77164" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{79}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f5561ca8a59b2eaedeef88d63f3cd36dea9b3abbe7b944cd99b6db533f584f7" "basis" 1409 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77164" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{82}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f5561ca8a59b2eaedeef88d63f3cd36dea9b3abbe7b944cd99b6db533f584f7" "basis" 1409 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-101512" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $a\\cdot b=-5$, find the angle between $a=⟨2t,t⟩$ and $b=⟨1,3⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f5561ca8a59b2eaedeef88d63f3cd36dea9b3abbe7b944cd99b6db533f584f7" "basis" 1409 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-101512" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, since $a\\cdot b=-5$, we can solve for $t$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =-5 \\\\ 2t\\cdot 1+t\\cdot 3 & =-5 \\\\ 2t+3t & =-5 \\\\ 5t & =-5 \\\\ t & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =⟨2(-1),\\,(-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $a$ and $b$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-5}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{3}^{2}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{5}\\cdot \\sqrt{10}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{5\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}})={135}^{∘}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f5561ca8a59b2eaedeef88d63f3cd36dea9b3abbe7b944cd99b6db533f584f7" "basis" 1409 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-101512" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6ec99b73bd0e45287c6205dca701f4d8435e073bd05cb9cfc6c557ae7078ee9b" "basis" 1409 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-101512" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/quest