/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f5561ca8a59b2eaedeef88d63f3cd36dea9b3abbe7b944cd99b6db533f584f7" "basis" 1409 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-101512" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{90}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f5561ca8a59b2eaedeef88d63f3cd36dea9b3abbe7b944cd99b6db533f584f7" "basis" 1409 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-101512" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{135}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f5561ca8a59b2eaedeef88d63f3cd36dea9b3abbe7b944cd99b6db533f584f7" "basis" 1409 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4327" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the angle between $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 2,-1,1 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 1,5,-2 \\rangle$. Round your answer to $1$ decimal place." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/example-4327.json" "file_sha256" "d54021ef644f7b5a247e30e2c3fc9eb3555b9bc1c406195f79d008067ba64e20" "basis" 1409 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4327" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Rearranging the dot product formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}+{a}_{z}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot 5+1\\cdot (-2)}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}}\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{5}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-5}{\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{30}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-5}{\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{5}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta = \\arccos \\left( -\\dfrac{\\sqrt{5}}{6} \\right) \\approx 111.9^\\circ.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/example-4327.json" "file_sha256" "d54021ef644f7b5a247e30e2c3fc9eb3555b9bc1c406195f79d008067ba64e20" "basis" 1409 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4328" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $\\angle BAC$ given the points $A(2,-1,-5)$, $B(-1,0,-4)$, and $C(5,1,1).$ Round your answer to $1$ decimal place." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/example-4328.json" "file_sha256" "c43feac91985f7b27ec8be206d554d465601616ddc293165e1174fd301ac5efc" "basis" 1409 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4328" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the position vectors of the points $A$, $B$, $C$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=⟨2,-1,-5⟩,\\,b=⟨-1,0,-4⟩,\\,c=⟨5,1,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $\\triangle ABC$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $\\angle BAC = \\theta.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/assets/285b8343208079181ac6036cf9ca16abc974d59b9262878ed40c0da9af5683d0.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,-4⟩-⟨2,-1,-5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,1,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =⟨5,1,1⟩-⟨2,-1,-5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,2,6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}}{|\\overset{\\to }{AB}||\\overset{\\to }{AC}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3\\cdot 3+1\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 6}{\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{6}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1}{\\sqrt{11}\\sqrt{49}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{7\\sqrt{11}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta = \\arccos \\left( -\\dfrac{1}{7\\sqrt{11}} \\right) \\approx 92.5^\\circ.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/example-4328.json" "file_sha256" "c43feac91985f7b27ec8be206d554d465601616ddc293165e1174fd301ac5efc" "basis" 1409 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-5112" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $\\mathbf{a}\\cdot \\mathbf{b}=-4$, find the angle between $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle t, \\, -2 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 6, \\, t \\rangle$. Round your answer to $1$ decimal place." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/example-5112.json" "file_sha256" "356ecf4df1339dc2a4c44a754ee592b1e87a838e992cfecdca401222768cfd31" "basis" 1409 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-5112" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, since $\\mathbf{a}\\cdot \\mathbf{b}=-4$, we can solve for $t$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =-4 \\\\ t\\cdot 6+(-2)\\cdot t & =-4 \\\\ 6t-2t & =-4 \\\\ 4t & =-4 \\\\ t & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=⟨-1,-2⟩,\\,b=⟨6,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+(-2)^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{{6}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{5}\\cdot \\sqrt{37}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{185}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta = \\arccos \\left( -\\dfrac{4}{\\sqrt{185}} \\right) \\approx 107.1^\\circ.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/example-5112.json" "file_sha256" "356ecf4df1339dc2a4c44a754ee592b1e87a838e992cfecdca401222768cfd31" "basis" 1409 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-101501" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the angle between $a=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Round your answer to $1$ decimal place." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b7539a42230fed6e2d9ff5ed5cf1cf5b9909132f751d2f82feeade76ad8478f"} {"question" "q-101501" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Rearranging the dot product formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 4+(-6)\\cdot 1}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-6)^{2}}\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{37}\\cdot \\sqrt{17}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{629}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{629}})≈{94.6}^{∘}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b7539a42230fed6e2d9ff5ed5cf1cf5b9909132f751d2f82feeade76ad8478f"} {"question" "q-101501" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "69439c99388ed4f03cb7c64633545f69bd84ad1aacf06d4f3cc7b3d16b3e60a7"} {"question" "q-101501" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b7539a42230fed6e2d9ff5ed5cf1cf5b9909132f751d2f82feeade76ad8478f"} {"question" "q-101501" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{102.1}^{∘}"] ["math" "{85.6}^{∘}"] ["math" "{89.9}^{∘}"] ["math" "{91.7}^{∘}"] ["math" "{94.6}^{∘}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b7539a42230fed6e2d9ff5ed5cf1cf5b9909132f751d2f82feeade76ad8478f"} {"question" "q-101501" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{94.6}^{∘}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b7539a42230fed6e2d9ff5ed5cf1cf5b9909132f751d2f82feeade76ad8478f"} {"question" "q-19028" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the angle between $a=⟨3,4⟩$ and $b=⟨-4,3⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b7539a42230fed6e2d9ff5ed5cf1cf5b9909132f751d2f82feeade76ad8478f"} {"question" "q-19028" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Rearranging the dot product formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\cdot (-4)+4\\cdot 3}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}}\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+{3}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{\\sqrt{25}\\cdot \\sqrt{25}} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(0)={90}^{∘}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b7539a42230fed6e2d9ff5ed5cf1cf5b9909132f751d2f82feeade76ad8478f"} {"question" "q-19028" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "69439c99388ed4f03cb7c64633545f69bd84ad1aacf06d4f3cc7b3d16b3e60a7"} {"question" "q-19028" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/